confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Stephanie Bice seeks a third term in a district that leans Republican by about nine points. She holds a commanding financial edge, with roughly $2 million on hand compared with about $17,000 for Democrat Jena Nelson, and carries a Trump endorsement. Expert raters overwhelmingly place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Nelson only about a 14 percent chance.\n\nThere are some signs of Democratic interest: national groups have signaled spending in the district, and a Democratic-sponsored September poll showed Nelson trailing by just five points. Still, with thin polling, Bice's resources, and the district's lean, the race remains firmly in Republican territory, with Nelson needing a substantial late shift to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}]}